<article class="crs-lesson">
    <h3><span class="crs-lesson-num">Lesson 2.1</span> Presenting Developments Clearly</h3>

    <span class="crs-sub-label">2.1.1 Buyers Buy a Lifestyle First</span>
    <p>Whether it's a master-planned subdivision in Cavite, a mid-rise condo in Quezon City, or a high-rise tower in BGC, buyers aren't just buying four walls — they're buying into a community and a lifestyle. Two units with the exact same floor plan can feel completely different to sell depending on what surrounds them, so your presentation has to zoom out before it zooms in.</p>
    <p>This matters even more in the Philippine market, where a large share of demand comes from OFWs and young professionals buying sight-unseen or on a single short trip home. For that buyer, the lifestyle story often has to do more work than the floor plan ever could, because they may never physically stand in the unit before deciding.</p>

    <span class="crs-sub-label">2.1.2 Three Things You Must Know Cold</span>
    <p>Tap each one to see why it matters.</p>
    <div class="crs-pin-grid" data-group="m2-know">
